WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.208
I chaired the economic council.

00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:23.000
It's called ECOFIN and it is kind of
the house of the 27 Member States.

00:00:23.166 --> 00:00:26.250
It's where ministers
from each country meet,

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:30.208
where compromises are made,
and when a compromise is made,

00:00:30.375 --> 00:00:33.208
on the basis of a proposal
from the Commission,

00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:36.375
then we will negotiate
with the European Parliament.

00:00:36.542 --> 00:00:38.041
It is a challenge.

00:00:38.208 --> 00:00:42.166
You are chairing a meeting
in another language with new colleagues

00:00:42.458 --> 00:00:47.208
and some of the issues that we are
debating are of a very complex nature.

00:00:47.375 --> 00:00:52.750
Interplay between the President chairing
it, the colleagues round the table

00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:58.792
and all the employees and staff
around us is very delicate.

00:00:59.166 --> 00:01:01.999
We had a very high priority file
from the Commission,

00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:05.542
concerning
how our financial institutions,

00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:07.875
how banks should work in future.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.166
There were
lots of different interests,

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:15.792
but there was also the momentum that
maybe we can reach an agreement today.

00:01:15.959 --> 00:01:21.583
The file we were negotiating over
for those 10–15 hours

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.250
contained, I think, 700 pages.

00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:29.417
So it is of crucial importance
that our staff have done their job.

00:01:30.375 --> 00:01:34.959
We had the meeting around the table.
We broke up. Had a break.

00:01:35.083 --> 00:01:37.458
Went into smaller meetings.

00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:40.875
People were coming and going,
discussing it in smaller groups.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.583
Back to the table to then figure out
how to take it from there.

00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:49.125
And the reason it took so long
was that we said:

00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:51.375
We are almost there now,
we are close.

00:01:51.542 --> 00:01:54.375
Maybe, maybe, maybe
we can reach a consensus today.

00:01:54.542 --> 00:01:56.667
We were getting very, very close.

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:58.834
In the end,
in the middle of the night,

00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:03.625
we had a consensus
among a huge qualified majority

00:02:03.792 --> 00:02:06.417
and we said: This is it.

00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:11.500
Now we have 14 days to make sure
that we got everything right.

00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:15.834
Negotiations always depend
on good preparation.

00:02:15.999 --> 00:02:17.667
Knowing what you want to achieve

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:21.458
but also knowing
where you can compromise.

